{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ClassicalRiemannHypothesis"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.classicalRiemannHypothesis_of_persistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.classicalRiemannHypothesis_of_persistence","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.lean#L76-L91","doc":"**The arc's claim, assembled.** Local critical-line alignment at every\nplace, together with adelic persistence, yields the classical Riemann\nhypothesis.\n\nThis is a genuine composition rather than the projection of a single\nassumption: it consumes the persistence class *and* a separate proof of local\nalignment, and neither alone gives the conclusion. It is the precise sense in\nwhich the framework \"reduces RH\" to its local statement — and it makes plain\nthat the reduction is only as strong as the persistence hypothesis, which is\nopen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.persistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.persistence","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Local alignment at every place implies the global critical-line property.\nStated as an implication so that the local hypothesis is visible in the\ntype: a proposition asserting only the conclusion would *be* RH, and one\nasserting only the antecedent would be a fact about the curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AdelicCriticalLinePersistence","kind":"class","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AdelicCriticalLinePersistence.lean#L53-L74","doc":"**Conjecture (adelic critical-line persistence).** If the local spectral\nexponents are critical-line aligned at every place, the global zeta function\ninherits the alignment: every non-trivial zero of `riemannZeta` has real part\n`1/2`.\n\n`P` indexes the places; `localSpectrum v` is the family of eight spectral\nexponents at the place `v`, in the sense of\n`QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.spectral_half_line` — whose conclusion `Re(ρ_i) = 1/2`\nis exactly this class's antecedent, and is well-posed because\n`spectral_coord_re_unique` makes that real part branch-independent.\n\nConjectural class — see\n[`conj:adelic-critical-line-persistence`](../../../quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/adelic-critical-line-persistence.md). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:adelic-critical-line-persistence","label":"conj:adelic-critical-line-persistence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/adelic-critical-line-persistence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}